## B. The budget decision (do not choose — inform the choice)

### B.1 Current state of the whole-system baseline: **red, in at least three independent places**

Measured on the current tree (HEAD `e1c65975` + working changes; the attribution runs and chainA run are dated 2026-09-29, i.e. current as of the latest tree content):

1. **Stage 4 (`bun run test`) — red.** 985 pass / **48 unique failures** / 7 errors (1033 tests, 303 files). All 48 measured **pre-existing at HEAD** (HEAD-source control run, identical name sets and assertion fingerprints): `dc-warn/out/stage4-attribution/REPORT.md`. Class split: **24 ASSERT + 24 TIMEOUT**. My own live rerun of one failing file today did not complete — bun 1.4.2 OOM-aborted (exit 134, peak ~6.7 GB; `evidence/spotcheck-oom.txt`) — so the live-reproduction datapoint is "harness itself fragile under load", and the authoritative current numbers remain the dated runs.
2. **Stage 3 (`driver-verify`, the 17-stage Option C chain) — red.** Full-chain attempt 2026-09-29 stopped at stage 3 rc=1: Swift library build rejected generated code (`cannot convert TiqianArray<GlyphMetrics> to [TiqianArray<GlyphMetrics>]`, root cause `SwiftArrayBoundary.hx:259` double wrap); 13 later stages never ran: `dc-warn/out/p09-chainA-full/REPORT.md`.
3. **After the (landed, uncommitted) PIT-255 fix, the *next* stage-3 blocker appears: cross-target consistency fails with 166 divergences** (f32 group): `dc-warn/out/swift-arrayboundary-fix/REPORT.md` §0/§6. Corresponding investigation is `doing` on the board (`investigate/f32-cross-target-divergence`), not signed off.
4. **Repairs exist only in scratch:** string-family fix (48→35 in its trees) and timeout-budget fix (48→25, zero timeouts) are validated patches in `dc-warn/out/…`, **not applied** to the inspected tree; both board tasks (`fix/rust-string-expectation-family`, `fix/test-timeout-budget`) are still `todo`.

So: the baseline is not "slightly red" — a candidate today cannot clear stage 3 (divergences), stage 4 (48 failures), or the P09 chain, and the two cheapest repairs (≈24 timeouts + stale expectations) are sitting integrated-and-verified in scratch.

### B.2 The decision, per CODEX-AUDIT §5

> "You cannot simultaneously require a bounded local change and expect it to erase an unrelated red whole-system baseline without budgeting that baseline work. Either fund their repair and enforce a stable candidate, or explicitly revise the programme's acceptance contract and publish what the narrower milestone means."

The repo's own rules make this forced: the work plan says a pre-existing/baseline failure "does not waive the standard" (`docs/architecture-work-plan.md`, verification rules — verified present), and P09 requires the candidate's *complete* required checks. Under the current contract, **P09 is unreachable until the baseline blockers above are repaired on a frozen candidate**. There is no third quiet option: treating baseline failures as exemptions would manufacture closure (AUDIT §2).

### B.3 Option 1 — Fund the baseline repair, enforce a stable candidate

Concrete committed work (bounded, mostly already de-risked):

| Work item | Est. character | Evidence it is understood |
|---|---|---|
| Integrate timeout-budget patch → new Stage-4 run | 48→~25 expected | validated patch, `test-timeout-budget/` |
| Integrate string-family fix (board task exists, `todo`) | ~25→~20 remaining ASSERT-class + 7 errors to triage | validated patch, `string-family-fix/` |
| Apply test-helper try/finally fix (`package-artifacts.test.ts`) | small code change; removes input-integrity confound | A8 above |
| Resolve 166 f32 divergences (or attribute them) | **open-ended; the one unbounded item** | `investigate/f32-cross-target-divergence` doing |
| Freeze one candidate, materialize input identity, full Option C re-run (17 stages) | mechanical but expensive (chainA wall-clock ≈ hours) | `p09-fixed-matrix-preparation-runbook.md`, done prep tasks |
| Tiqian side: pinned `8504d23`, 12 generation + 11 target-test obligations | **availability unverified (A26) — the hard unknown** | runbook + `tiqian-preparation-review.md` |

Consequences: P09 becomes genuinely reachable; P10/P12 keep their current meaning; cost is dominated by the divergence item and one full-chain run per candidate; every scratch patch re-enters as a *new input state* requiring fresh runs (repo rule).

### B.4 Option 2 — Revise the acceptance contract, publish the narrower milestone

What revising actually commits the owner to (not just wording):

- Write down which failures are *out of scope* for P09, as an explicit list with revisions (e.g. "the 48 Stage-4 names at `e1c65975` are baseline, tracked as governance tasks, not P09 blockers"), and amend the "does not waive the standard" clause or scope it.
- Accept that P09 then certifies a **narrower claim** (e.g. "stage-3 generation + Swift leg green; cross-target comparison reported, not gating"), and P10/P12 must publish that narrower meaning — the audit says an interim audit "would not justify closing the goal" without this.
- Carry the reputational/traceability cost: the gates were the programme's own definition of done; weakening them after 50+ rounds is exactly the "relabel implementation violation as accepted" move the audit warns against (AUDIT §2, RECORD critique) — it must therefore be a *scope* decision, not an *evidence* decision.
- Cost saved: potentially weeks of baseline repair and the divergence investigation; P08's focused acceptance is **already compatible with either option** (focused P08 acceptance precedes P09 under both).

### B.5 What the decider needs in order to choose

1. The list above (B.1) — what exactly is red and what each repair costs.
2. Whether the 166 divergences are a bounded f32 issue or a class of unknown size (currently `doing`, unsigned-off — this is the single biggest cost unknown in Option 1).
3. Whether Tiqian at `8504d23` is actually runnable locally or in an authorized environment (A26 — currently unestablished; if truly unavailable, Option 1's P09 completion is externally blocked regardless of budget).
4. Whether any consumer of P09's verdict needs the full-system claim, or whether the narrower claim suffices.

**Not chosen here.** Both options are coherent; Option 1 buys the original contract at a measurable price; Option 2 buys speed at the price of publishing a weaker milestone. The one prohibited path is the implicit one (current default).

